Z||000000||fierogt88||01-26-2001||10:52 AM||||I have a line on a 3.4 from a 96 camaro cheap with medium miles...  but I seem to remember that we use the 93-95 3.4's?  What's the difference?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula 18||01-26-2001||11:26 AM||||The 96 Camaro used a the 3800 series. It has a 90 degree 3.8L v6. You want one the had the 3.4L 60 degree v6.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierogt88||01-26-2001||11:10 PM||||Hmmmm.... quite strange.  I called the guy and he insists that it is out of a 1996 camaro and it is a 3.4L HO FI engine.  also comes with a 5 spd trans for $500  only 14k.  I need to know for sure cuz this seems like a deal to me...  were there any 3.4's in 96??  could this be a last 3.4 off the line or something?||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||01-27-2001||12:40 AM||||There were no 3.4's in '96, so he may be mistaken on the years.<P>I just pulled some parts off of a '93 Fiero, if you believe what the junkyard scribbled on the windsheld.  As long as it is a 3.4 from a Camaro youll be OK.  The differences bewteen the 3.4 and 3800 are obvious, so you can't possibly mix them up.<P>I'd say grab it.....$500 is a steal.  Does that include the tranny?  You could sell it to recoup some of your investment.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||01-27-2001||10:19 AM||||For $500 I would definatly go for it! He is probally just mistaken on years. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula 18||01-27-2001||11:47 AM||||The 3.4 Is pretty easy to spot. I think it even says 3.4 right on the manifold. %00 is a great price for the miles. I'd say take a tlook at it and grab it if it is a 3.4. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierogt88||01-29-2001||11:20 AM||||Ok.  It is a 3.4.  He insists that it came out of his friends 96 camaro, but it was a year ago and his friend is gone so I'm betting it was a 95...  Before I grab this engine though, I need to know something.<P>This is the engine that needs the new holes drilled for the starter.  How and where would I get this done?  about how much should that cost?  and wouldn't I need some sort of drilling guide/template?  where could I get one of these?||||reg||5
Z||000007||tgowens||01-29-2001||11:27 AM||||we have the drill guide here at the shop - call George at the shop at 510-233-4376<P>And, if it is the 3.4 pushrod engine from the Camaro rear wheel drive '93 - '95 you have the right one........||||reg||1
